GOVERNMENT OF KARNATAKA
RIGHT TO INFORMATION ACT, 2005
RTI RESPONSE - FIRST INFORMATION OFFICER
Office of the Commissioner, BBMP

RTI Application Reference: BBMP/RTI/2024/W150/00234
Applicant: Mr. Rajesh Kumar Nair, Ward 150 Resident
Application Date: 10-January-2024
Response Date: 05-February-2024 (within 30-day statutory limit)

------------------------------------------------------------------
INFORMATION SOUGHT
------------------------------------------------------------------
The applicant has sought the following information under Section 6 of the Right to Information Act, 2005:

1. Total funds allocated and spent on Ward 150 infrastructure for FY 2022-23 and FY 2023-24
2. Status of Bellandur Lake rejuvenation project and funds utilised
3. Details of road maintenance contracts awarded in Ward 150 since 2020
4. Details of any pending land acquisition notices in Ward 150

------------------------------------------------------------------
REPLY OF THE PUBLIC INFORMATION OFFICER
------------------------------------------------------------------

QUERY 1: INFRASTRUCTURE FUNDS - WARD 150

FY 2022-23 ALLOCATION AND EXPENDITURE:
- Allocated: Rs. 14.2 crore (BBMP Annual Budget, Ward 150 Head)
- Spent: Rs. 9.1 crore (64.1% utilisation)
- Unspent balance lapsed: Rs. 5.1 crore (returned to consolidated fund)

FY 2023-24 ALLOCATION AND EXPENDITURE (till 31-December-2023):
- Allocated: Rs. 16.8 crore
- Spent: Rs. 6.3 crore (37.5% utilisation as of date of this response)
- Pending utilisation: Rs. 10.5 crore

NOTE: The Public Information Officer notes that 38.6% of the FY 2022-23 budget for storm water drain maintenance (Rs. 3.2 crore) was not utilised due to contractor default under Contract No. BBMP/ENG/SWD/2022/089. The contractor (M/s Srinivasa Construction) was blacklisted vide BBMP Order dated 14-November-2022.

QUERY 2: BELLANDUR LAKE REJUVENATION PROJECT

The Bellandur Lake Rejuvenation project is being implemented in two phases:

Phase 1 (2019-2023):
- Sanctioned amount: Rs. 45.7 crore (Joint funding: BBMP Rs. 28 crore + World Bank grant Rs. 17.7 crore)
- Spent: Rs. 41.3 crore
- Status: PARTIALLY COMPLETE. Storm water drain desilting and shoreline stabilisation completed (90%). Floating wetlands installation delayed due to land encroachment dispute on Survey No. 34/A. 3.4 acres of lake area remains under illegal encroachment. Eviction order under Section 61 of Karnataka Land Revenue Act issued on 12-September-2023. Matter pending before Karnataka High Court (WP No. 44521/2023).

Phase 2 (Proposed 2024-2027):
- Estimated cost: Rs. 68 crore
- Status: Awaiting State Government budget approval. Not yet sanctioned.

QUERY 3: ROAD MAINTENANCE CONTRACTS

Road maintenance contracts awarded in Ward 150 since 2020:

1. Contract BBMP/RD/2020/W150/012 - White-topping of 3.2 km internal roads
   Contractor: M/s Ramaiah Infraprojects | Value: Rs. 4.8 crore | Status: COMPLETED (2021)

2. Contract BBMP/RD/2022/W150/034 - Pothole repair and road re-carpeting (monsoon damage)
   Contractor: M/s Karnataka Road Contractors Association | Value: Rs. 1.9 crore
   Status: COMPLETED with defects noted. Quality audit report BBMP/QA/2022/089 flagged 34% of repaired stretches as sub-standard. Contractor issued cure notice.

3. Contract BBMP/RD/2023/W150/061 - Outer Ring Road service road repairs (2.1 km)
   Contractor: M/s Deccan Infrastructure Ltd | Value: Rs. 3.2 crore | Status: IN PROGRESS
   Expected completion: 30-April-2024.

QUERY 4: PENDING LAND ACQUISITION NOTICES

As of the date of this response, the following land acquisition proceedings are active in Ward 150:

1. BBMP Road Widening Acquisition (ORR Extension):
   - Notice Reference: BBMP/LA/2024/W150/001
   - Area proposed for acquisition: 8.2 metres both sides of ORR, Bellandur to Sarjapur (4.2 km)
   - Survey Numbers affected: 28, 29, 30, 31, 42, 43, 44, 67, 68, 71, 72, 78, 82, 83 of Bellandur Village
   - Estimated affected structures: 287 buildings
   - Compensation basis: Karnataka Guidance Value (last revised 2023)
   - Status: PRELIMINARY NOTIFICATION issued. Objection period active (deadline 30-April-2024).

2. BDA Zoning Reclassification Notice:
   - Notice Reference: BDA/ZR/2024/150/0892
   - Area: Survey numbers 42, 43, 44, 67, 68 of Bellandur Village
   - Proposed change: Mixed Residential (MR-2) to Commercial (C-2) zone
   - Status: PUBLIC NOTICE ISSUED. Objection deadline 30 days from gazette notification.

